  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Production of feed-grade copper sulphate</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Procesadora Elvira is a Bolivian manufacturer of sulphuric acid and copper sulphate for the local mining industry. Together with their partner Chilean Copper Ltda, Procesadora Elvira identified a good market opportunity for high quality feed-grade copper sulphate in Canada and the USA. The joint venture company will produce feed-grade copper sulphate as feed additive, by using its surplus sulphuric acid and recycling locally collected copper scrap and abandoned ore with low copper content.A pilot plant with up-to-date, environmentally sound technology will be set up in Oruro. The project will present a solution for the current bad practice of burning plasticised copper wire by the scrap collectors. The joint venture will sign long-term supply contracts with the scrap dealers, under the condition that the copper wire will be supplied including the plastic. The company will separate the plastic from the copper through an environmentally friendly mechanical process, after which the plastic will be sold for recycling purposes. Further, it will train the collectors and the small-scale mining companies on prevention of child and forced labour and on environmental care. The company will be certified according to ISO 9001, ISO 14001 and OHSAS 18001.</narrative>
  </description>
